{
  "analysis": "The file graphene.dat is a 2-column space-separated text file using comma as the decimal separator (European format): column 1 is monotonic decreasing (so it's the x-axis), column 2 is the intensity (y). Values range roughly x from 47183 down to 1648. Before fitting, I must (1) install numpy and scipy, and (2) convert the comma decimals to dots so numpy can read it. I need to first explore the data to locate the actual peaks, since the G peak hint (~1580) is near the edge of the data range.",
  "plan": "First confirm python/pip. Then install numpy and scipy. After that I'll write an exploration script to load the data (replacing commas with dots), sort by x, and locate the dominant peaks to understand where G and 2D peaks sit. This guides the fitting.",
